: \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"b894aac5c23bd9b2dd516a5c61ab63b3df7da0f97afad1d7071f3c3b3349cbec","event_uuid":"6a1dcb48-dbec-4a66-9bd3-8fdd231bcebf","position":{"commit_sha":"91a5904f4863238228900519d9dfe4d82ce5d69d","position":"1787868381533150001-6a1dcb48-dbec-4a66-9bd3-8fdd231bcebf"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"2e7eb21cce38edddaf1d8b066fa23388750bf34162c4654c9bcc1ec432f93050","event_uuid":"7f0312e8-12fe-4431-b272-3d47a3351c5b","position":{"commit_sha":"83bccecb02c1bb749cf1a8a2954df581066db0f5","position":"1787869345474595001-7f0312e8-12fe-4431-b272-3d47a3351c5b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"d9ad31c3aa88eadd701da293720e4a99d50e56c5fbcc0b3099311ff118a2222a","event_uuid":"4ffcf634-b3ff-4149-baec-839aa5434361","position":{"commit_sha":"619a0552dd0a94b148b088abb7c3bed196cd0aa3","position":"1787869720513752001-4ffcf634-b3ff-4149-baec-839aa5434361"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"54cc2745d18013b49a206c922fd6b0e2c2de2cfd9c6bf55ac5dd6731400a1193","event_uuid":"0fda508a-983e-405c-973f-41e56368a3e3","position":{"commit_sha":"619a0552dd0a94b148b088abb7c3bed196cd0aa3","position":"1787869722167577001-0fda508a-983e-405c-973f-41e56368a3e3"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787866276700841118,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"7f0312e8-12fe-4431-b272-3d47a3351c5b","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"524d-22a5-1a21-49d7"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nThe reducer stamps the claim-session provenance (`claimed_session`, `claim_harness`,\n`claim_remote_session`) **only** on the winning `open -> in_progress` STATUS fold —\n`_fold_claimed_session` (`src/rebar/reducer/_processors_status.py:25`), keyed on\n`current_status == \"open\" and status == \"in_progress\"`. Nothing ever clears it, so a\nticket that has left `in_progress` (closed / blocked / re-opened) still reports the last\nclaimer's session (documented behaviour, `docs/event-schema.md:250-255`). For the\ncross-session warning (this ticket's parent) to mean \"currently `in_progress` by session\nX\", the provenance must be **cleared on every exit from `in_progress`**.\n\nA consumer scan confirms this is behaviour-safe: every reader of these three keys is pure\npassthrough — the LLM compact-key map (`src/rebar/reducer/llm_format.py:44-46`\n`csn`/`chn`/`rsn`), the MCP model fields (`src/rebar/_mcp_models.py:109-111`), the state\ndefaults (`src/rebar/reducer/_state.py:47-49`), the `TicketState` typing\n(`src/rebar/types.py:123-125`), and the `txn.py` writer. Nothing branches on the value or\nrelies on it persisting past `in_progress`.\n\n## Approach\n\nIn `src/rebar/reducer/_processors_status.py`, add a sibling helper (e.g.\n`_clear_claimed_session(state)`) that sets `state[\"claimed_session\"]`,\n`state[\"claim_harness\"]`, and `state[\"claim_remote_session\"]` to `None`, and invoke it on\na winning STATUS fold where `data[\"current_status\"] == \"in_progress\"` and\n`data[\"status\"] != \"in_progress\"`. Invoke it in the **same two branches** where\n`_fold_claimed_session` is applied — the normal-update branch\n(`_processors_status.py:166`) and the fork-**winner** branch (`:139`) — and **never** in\nthe branch where the existing chain wins, so a losing concurrent transition cannot clear\nthe fork winner's provenance (mirrors the `_fold_claimed_session` fork-winner gating,\nadvisory G6/T8). The clear and the set are mutually exclusive per event (an event is\neither entering or leaving `in_progress`), so ordering is irrelevant.\n\nThis is additive and forward/back-compatible: older clones ignore reducer-state shape;\n`make_initial_state` already defaults these three keys to `None`\n(`src/rebar/reducer/_state.py:47-49`), so a fresh replay and a snapshot-served state\nagree, and a pre-feature SNAPSHOT that lacks a post-exit clear simply restores whatever it\nstored (no migration of stored events — state is recomputed from the append-only log).\nRollback is trivial: reverting the reducer change restores the prior persist-past-exit\nbehaviour with no stored-data cleanup, because no event bytes change.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/reducer/_processors_status.py` — add the clear helper + invoke on the exit\n  edge in the normal-update and fork-winner branches.\n- `docs/event-schema.md` — document, in §\"Session provenance (`claimed_session`)\", that\n  the three fields are cleared on every exit from `in_progress` (so a non-`in_progress`\n  ticket reports no holder).\n\nNo new event type, no schema change (the keys already exist), no config.\n\n## Testing\n\nTier: **in-process unit test against the real reducer** replaying real event sequences\n(test-design §3 \"pure calculation / validation branch\" — the whole mechanism is the\nreducer fold; no CLI/git/process boundary is crossed). Existing reducer tests live under\n`tests/` next to the other `_processors`/reducer suites; inventory those first and extend\nthe nearest claim-session suite rather than duplicating fixtures.\n\n- Happy path + collateral: replay `open -> in_progress` with `data[\"session\"]=\"A\"`,\n  `data[\"harness\"]=\"claude-code\"`, `data[\"remote_session\"]=\"R\"`, then `in_progress ->\n  closed`; assert the reduced state has all three of `claimed_session`, `claim_harness`,\n  `claim_remote_session` equal to `None`.\n- Parameterized exit edges: the same three-field clear holds for `in_progress -> blocked`,\n  `in_progress -> open`, and `in_progress -> idea` (one parameterized case per status).\n- Negative control (behavior must NOT change): `open -> in_progress` with **no** later\n  exit leaves `claimed_session == \"A\"` (and the two siblings set) — proves the change\n  only clears on exit, not on entry.\n- Fork gating: given a STATUS fork on the exit edge, a **losing** concurrent\n  `in_progress -> closed` event does not clear the fork-**winner**'s `claimed_session`\n  (the winner keeps its holder); assert against the lexical-UUID winner already used by\n  `_fold_claimed_session`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Replaying `open->in_progress(session=A,harness=claude-code,remote_session=R)` then\n  `in_progress->closed` yields reduced state with `claimed_session`, `claim_harness`,\n  `claim_remote_session` all `None` (checked by a new reducer test, e.g.\n  `test_claim_session_cleared_on_close`, run under `make test`).\n- [ ] Replaying `open->in_progress(session=A)` then `in_progress->blocked` yields\n  `claimed_session is None` (checked by the parameterized reducer test case\n  `test_claim_session_cleared_on_exit[blocked]`).\n- [ ] Replaying `open->in_progress(session=A)` then `in_progress->open` yields\n  `claimed_session is None` (checked by the parameterized reducer test case\n  `test_claim_session_cleared_on_exit[open]`).\n- [ ] Replaying `open->in_progress(session=A)` then `in_progress->idea` yields\n  `claimed_session is None` (checked by the parameterized reducer test case\n  `test_claim_session_cleared_on_exit[idea]`).\n- [ ] Negative control: `open->in_progress` with no subsequent exit leaves\n  `claimed_session==\"A\"` (checked by a reducer test asserting the field persists while\n  `in_progress`).\n- [ ] A losing concurrent exit STATUS in a fork does not clear the fork-winner's\n  `claimed_session` (checked by a reducer fork test asserting the winner's holder is\n  intact).\n- [ ] `docs/event-schema.md` §\"Session provenance\" gains the sentence stating the three\n  fields are cleared on every exit from `in_progress` (checked:\n  `grep -nE \"cleared on every exit from .in_progress.\" docs/event-schema.md` matches the\n  new sentence, and it sits under the §\"Session provenance\" heading).","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/reducer/_processors_status.py","reason":"add a clear helper and invoke it on the in_progress->exit edge in the normal-update and fork-winner branches"},{"path":"docs/event-schema.md","reason":"document that claim-session provenance is cleared on every exit from in_progress"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","1aca-695f-a0a4-4236"],["relates_to","524d-22a5-1a21-49d7"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"1aca-695f-a0a4-4236","parent_status_uuid":"4ffcf634-b3ff-4149-baec-839aa5434361","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"6f74-2795-5ad4-4a56","ticket_type":"story","title":"Clear claim-session provenance on every exit from in_progress (reducer)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["f63052e8-19f6-4c76-9224-498904565a48","7b853760-b0d0-40cc-9083-5386de86f9a9","58550836-73b2-4008-af51-f392b8967bcc","b9391026-3379-4eaf-8a80-d77d52fd5f44","6a1dcb48-dbec-4a66-9bd3-8fdd231bcebf","7f0312e8-12fe-4431-b272-3d47a3351c5b","4ffcf634-b3ff-4149-baec-839aa5434361","0fda508a-983e-405c-973f-41e56368a3e3"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787869722167577002,"uuid":"ac2b7204-508a-4273-ae95-035c1e8df65b"}